  "currents": [
    {
      "name": "The Mild Current",
      "warm": true,
      "_why": "A warm ocean current (like the Gulf Stream) flows north-east across the western ocean from the subtropics, past the western isles and up the west coast of Sellador, then (author: it does not split) straight through the strait between Tel-Tenauril (north) and Sellador (south) into the Inner Sea, ending near Baratoria. It is why Sellador, Gideon and Midland have an English/French climate at that latitude, why Lochlainn is lush, and why the western isles are subtropical. The strait runs along world y~214-218 from x~10 to x~120.",
